=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play updates/crond-shared ------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/crond-shared$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23 (OpenRC). crond running$
# and at boot before hardn, logrotate's daily job, then hardn's$
# Enable. Disable removes apk-cron and keeps crond, saying why.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured apk-cron$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  apk-cron             Installed$
   -  Daily Script         In place /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
   -  crond                Running starts at boot$
   -  Other Jobs           logrotate use crond$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
  Checking the host...$
$
# Disable automatic updates ####################################$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         Off$
   -  crond                Kept running before hardn$
   -  Rollback             Reinstalls from the repositories$
$
   -  Remove apk-cron$
      apk-cron$
      $ apk del apk-cron$
$
   -  Delete hardn's record$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates off? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Remove apk-cron        Done$
  [+] Delete hardn's record  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no apk-cron$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] apk-cron             Not installed$
   -  crond                Running starts at boot$
   -  Other Jobs           logrotate use crond$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Daily, by apk-cron$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: updates/crond-shared$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on$
# web-01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order;$
# hardn's own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Before the first change$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ apk del --simulate apk-cron$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ apk del --simulate apk-cron$
$
   -  Applied: Remove apk-cron$
      /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
      $ apk del apk-cron$
      $ rc-service crond status$
$

